From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Venus Build Fix <noreply@example.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 13:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bcm2711_defconfig: disable the cpuset cgroup v1 legacy
 interface

Mainline Linux has no Kconfig option to remove core cgroup v1 mount
support entirely (kernel/cgroup/cgroup-v1.o is built unconditionally,
obj-y in kernel/cgroup/Makefile) - v1-vs-v2 is a runtime choice, made
via the cgroup_no_v1= boot parameter, not a compile-time one. What
Kconfig does offer is disabling the *legacy-only* per-controller
interface where a controller has one. CONFIG_MEMCG_V1 is already off
in this defconfig (by its own Kconfig default, nothing explicitly
disabled it). CONFIG_CPUSETS_V1 is the only other such toggle in this
kernel version and is currently on - disable it to match, for
container workloads that only need the unified (v2) hierarchy.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Venus specific]

---
 arch/arm64/configs/bcm2711_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/configs/bcm2711_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/bcm2711_defconfig
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@
 CONFIG_CGROUP_PIDS=y
 CONFIG_CGROUP_FREEZER=y
 CONFIG_CPUSETS=y
-CONFIG_CPUSETS_V1=y
+# CONFIG_CPUSETS_V1 is not set
 CONFIG_CGROUP_DEVICE=y
 CONFIG_CGROUP_CPUACCT=y
 CONFIG_CGROUP_PERF=y
